  "steps": [
    "Season the chicken cutlets on both sides with the kosher salt, garlic powder, onion powder, black pepper and paprika.",
    "Set up three shallow bowls: whisk the dry dredge ingredients in the first, the eggs, pickle brine and cream in the second, and the breadcrumbs, Parmesan and basil in the third.",
    "Heat about 2 in of oil in a large heavy pot or Dutch oven over medium-high heat to 350°F. Set a wire rack over a rimmed sheet pan.",
    "Dredge each cutlet in the flour mixture and shake off the excess, dip it in the egg wash and let the excess drip off, then press it firmly into the Parmesan breadcrumbs on both sides.",
    "Fry 2 or 3 cutlets at a time, 4 to 5 min per side, until deep golden brown and an instant-read thermometer reads 165°F in the thickest part. Drain on the rack and let the oil come back to 350°F between batches.",
    "Preheat the oven to 425°F. Mix the melted butter, garlic, parsley, Parmesan and salt, and brush it generously over the cut sides of the baguettes.",
    "Set the baguettes cut side up on a sheet pan and bake 6 to 8 min, until golden and toasted at the edges.",
    "Whisk all the Caesar dressing ingredients together, then toss with the chopped romaine right before serving.",
    "Cut each baguette into 3 pieces. Build each sandwich with 2 crispy cutlets and a pile of Caesar salad, and serve right away."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Pickle brine in the egg wash seasons the crust.",
    "The dressing makes about 2 1/2 cups, more than the salad needs. Spread the extra on the baguettes or keep it covered in the fridge."
  ],
